  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Throw-out, drop pass and 2v1",
  "description": "Three groups: A and B attack, C defends. The coach stands in the near goal as goalkeeper with the balls, and a goalkeeper is in the far goal. C waits just outside the centre circle.\n\nThe coach throws the ball out to A, who skates towards it. At the same time B swings round in a wide arc and arrives at speed. A drops the ball back towards their own goal to B, who carries it upfield with the speed. A turns and joins. A and B play 2v1 against C and finish. Rotation: A goes to B, B to C and C to A.\n\nSwitch sides after a while. Encourage creativity in the attack – give-and-go, crossing runs, dummies. On a big rink the coach can throw out from the centre circle instead. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "B skates a proper arc so they are at full speed when the ball is dropped back."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "A drops the ball back and to the side, so B can take it without slowing down."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "In the 2v1: skate at the defender and pass when they commit."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "C tries to steer the ball carrier towards the board while keeping an eye on the other attacker."
    }
  ],
